Z||000000||Alan Surber||11-01-2000||02:44 PM||||When timing gears strip at freeway speeds, what is the likelyhood of bent valves?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||11-01-2000||03:06 PM||||I believe both the V6 and I4 are non-interference engines.  Other than a car that suddenly stops running and a lot of work afterwards, you shouldn't have a problem...<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 151,000 miles and counting!         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">      <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||11-01-2000||03:55 PM||||I have had the timing gear on my Duke shed its teeth at highway speeds not once, but twice!  Other than the aggrevation of having to tear things apart to change the camshaft gear, there were no other problems.  I highly recommend replacing the fiber cam gear with an all steel gear so that the problem doesn't recurr.  I don't know about the six, I've heard that some bend valves and some don't.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE||||reg||12
